      en: "The Guelta of Matmata is a permanent waterhole in the Adrar region of Mauritania, located in a rocky canyon. It is fed by groundwater and provides essential water for wildlife in the arid environment. The guelta is frequented by gazelles, baboons, and birds. Nearby rock paintings date from the Neolithic period. The water depth ranges from 1 to 3 meters depending on season.",
